    "why_change": "10% is too cautious as the sole central ASP assumption given the observed premium-family ramp, a higher late-2026 price level and further Clearwater/Diamond adoption. The two prior years also show that mix and customer composition can reverse ASPs, so 54% YoY is not repeated. Growth decelerates sharply after 2027 as comparisons toughen and mix penetration matures.",
    "why_not_claim_exact_carryover": "Published rounded YoY unit/ASP changes and rounded non-server revenue do not identify absolute quarterly shipments or Q4 2026 exit ASP. No percentage-point decomposition between carryover, same-SKU pricing and richer mix is presented as measured.",
    "incremental_profit": "Extra server sales relative to the paired host receive 50% incremental consolidated operating profit through 2030, after all direct input/production/operating costs and D&A. This allowance is recorded in Products for calculation, with the existing dollar Foundry profit path held unchanged. It is not a prediction of reported segment attribution.",
    "profit_rationale": "Q3 2026 DCAI revenue increased about $3.2B and product profit about $2.2B after premium-product unit costs, implying roughly 69% incremental product-profit retention. The observed 41.5% segment operating margin is an average, not the margin on extra ASP. A 50% forward allowance recognizes leverage on the same package count while reserving material cost for larger/more complex silicon, new-node ramp and supplier pass-through. It is below the observed bridge but not justified merely as conservatism.",
    "foundry_boundary": "Do not add separate manufacturing learning, higher internal-transfer profit, cost reductions or fixed-cost absorption to the unchanged Foundry dollar path. Actual incremental earnings could be reported partly in Foundry. The 50% consolidated allowance already captures the net result once.",
    "physical_capex_2027_2030_B": [
      29,
      31,
      30,
      29
    ],
    "capital_rationale": "The paired policy already retained the funded-bull $29B/$31B capacity budgets in 2027/28 despite fewer package units. Richer dies/package can use that capacity. Restore the $1B removed in each of 2029 and 2030, returning to the funded-bull physical budget; do not call the richer mix physically free. Exact good-die/substrate capacity per dollar is not disclosed, so this remains an owned aggregate allowance.",
    "DA_rule": "Retain 14/16.5B total D&A in 2027/28. The extra $1B physical investments in each of 2029/30 are assigned an eight-year life with half-year convention, adding 0.0625B/0.1875B D&A in those years. Starting 2031 the existing aggregate D&A/Products-revenue normalization, 18.5/19/19.5/19.75/20% to 2035 and 20% thereafter, applies to revised Products sales and replaces the explicit incremental cohort approximation; do not add both.",
    "WC_rule": "For 2027\u201330 preserve the paired supplier/operating cash uses plus 10% of each year change in incremental server sales. From 2031 retain 10% of total host external-sales change.",
    "continuation": "From 2031 retain the paired unit and ASP growth rates on the revised level. Incremental EBIT retention declines linearly from 50% in 2030 to 32% in 2040, then holds 32%. No permanent 50% premium is capitalized. Host incremental sales/net operating investment remains 0.80 including WC; gross physical capex = D&A + change in host external sales / 0.80 - change in WC. All categories grow 3% nominal from 2041 with stable margins and funded investment.",
    "unmodified": "Client, Other DCAI, corporate, taxes, credits, capitalized financing interest, leases, NCI, claims and separate external-packaging policy remain under their existing owners. No automatic new subsidy/customer financing. Packaging sales are excluded from host capital turnover."
  },
