  "falsifiers_and_m37_use": {
    "claim": "Package-unit share understates the revenue opportunity when CPU content and realized value per package rise. A20% unit forecast can coexist with much stronger server revenue; the investment question is retained profit after physical and capital costs.",
    "nearest_falsifier": "Quarterly server ASP stops rising as additional Ireland/substrate supply arrives, or unit growth comes primarily from discounted lower-core hyperscaler SKUs rather than premium-family penetration. A delayed Diamond ramp weakens2028 ASP most directly.",
    "positive_update": "Accepted premium-family shipment growth with stable per-core pricing, rising absolute gross profit and delivery growth without disproportionate wafer/substrate investment would support more than this selected50% retention.",
    "strongest_objection": "Granite is already the largest family, so part of the mix transition has happened; high-core products can reduce the package count needed per workload. AMD/Arm competition and customer discounts may prevent today\u2019s scarcity rent from surviving supply expansion. The2024\u201325 ASP reversal is direct evidence against perpetual scarcity.",
    "rules_source": "https://www.m37.com/spc2026",
